    <statement><p>The plane <m>y=1</m> intersects the surface <m>z=x^{4}+4xy-y^{7}</m> in a certain curve. Find the slope of the tangent line of this curve at the point <m>P=(1,1,4)</m>.</p>
<p><m>m=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>z=z(x,1)=x^{4}+4x-1</m>, obtained by intersecting the surface <m>z=x^{4}+4xy-y^{7}</m> with the plane <m>y=1</m>, is the partial derivative <m>\frac {\partial{z}}{\partial{x}}(1,1)</m>.



 <m>\frac {\partial{z}}{\partial{x}}=\frac {\partial}{\partial{x}}\left( x^{4}+4xy-y^{7} \right) = 4x^{3}+4y</m>



<m>m=\frac {\partial{z}}{\partial{x}}(1,1)=4 \cdot 1^{3}+4 \cdot 1=8</m>





</solution>
